  published jar does not carry. Nothing in it is compiled or patched.

raylib examples
---------------
  Copyright (c) 2013-2026 Ramon Santamaria (@raysan5) and contributors
  Licensed under the zlib/libpng license.

  The example programs under raylib-examples/src/raylib_examples/ are ports
  of raylib's own example programs to jank. They are altered versions: the
  logic is reimplemented in jank, and the interop constraints described in
  docs/guide/ forced structural changes throughout. Every example's docstring
  names the upstream C source it was ported from (e.g. core/core_basic_window,
  shapes/shapes_bouncing_ball), and raylib-examples/README.md lists the same
  mapping in table form.

  One deliberate behavioural deviation from the originals, applied uniformly:
  every example sets FLAG_WINDOW_HIGHDPI.

rlights.h
---------
  Copyright (c) 2017-2024 Victor Fisac (@victorfisac) and
                          Ramon Santamaria (@raysan5)
  Licensed under the zlib/libpng license.

  jank-raylib-sys/include/jank_rlights.h is an altered version of raylib's
  examples/shaders/rlights.h. CreateLight and UpdateLightValues are kept
  verbatim from the original and marked static; the surrounding index-based
  scalar wrappers and per-type uniform setters are new work, needed because
  jank functions can neither take nor return native values. The file's own
  header comment carries the same attribution.

